    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2y-1,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2y-1\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 2y-1 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\u27e82y-1,y\u27e9,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "8f35ee4c-844a-5251-8f46-78931db9c1ba",
